    {
      "because": "the rule makes no claim between an offer that published a salary and one that did not, so the tiebreak the rule drives may make none either; sorting the silent side last reads the absence as a low number, and at 97 bands in 561 offers that buries four offers in five beneath every tied offer from a board that publishes",
      "case": "an_absent_salary_keeps_the_place_the_alphabet_gave_it",
      "claiming_pairs_broken_when_reversed": 0,
      "incomparable_pairs_clean_in_either_order": 1,
      "pairs": 1,
      "pay_dominance_claimed": 0,
      "violations": 0
    },
    {
      "because": "a point is the band whose ends coincide, so a claim is made only when the two bands are disjoint; across currencies there is no claim at all, because converting needs a rate with a date and a source and none lives in this repository",
